## 1. Additional permission for the TAK Software (section 7)

An ATAK plugin is loaded into ATAK's own process and calls ATAK's API directly.
That is what a plugin is, and the license was not written with it in mind, so
the permission below is granted explicitly.

> **Additional permission under __LICENSE_SHORT__ section 7**
>
> As a special exception, the copyright holders of __DISPLAY__ give you permission to
> combine, link with, and distribute __DISPLAY__, or a work based on __DISPLAY__, together
> with the TAK Software (ATAK-CIV, ATAK-GOV, ATAK-MIL and the TAK Software
> Development Kit, as licensed by the United States Government under the TAK
> Software License Agreement) and to convey the resulting work.
>
> You must still comply with the __LICENSE_SHORT__ in all respects for the portions of the
> resulting work that are __DISPLAY__, or a work based on __DISPLAY__.
>
> If you modify this file, you may extend this exception to your version of the
> file, but you are not obliged to do so. If you do not wish to do so, delete this
> exception statement from your version.

**In plain English.** You can build this plugin against the TAK SDK, sideload it
into ATAK, and hand the result to whoever you like, without anyone claiming the
license reaches into ATAK. What stays covered is this plugin's own source.

**If you only install and use __DISPLAY__, none of this touches you.**

**This exception does not come from the Government, and does not change the TAK
Software License Agreement.** It is __HOLDER__ removing a restriction its own
license would otherwise impose.

